>Galtra the elvish ranger has just finished the quest, and has a large
>abundance of weapons and missiles, but no ways of polymorphing. Which
>of these are best for use during the castle? She has an unused magic
>marker to use on enchant weapon scrolls so no problem their. She also
>has a reasonable HP and AC, no pet, magic resitance, reflection,
>invisibility, crowned, displacement, ESP, maxed stats, basically full
>Asecention kit except for a decent weapon.
>
>The choices are:
>
>Elven bow + 200 elven arrows (Only used 10 in the mines, and saved the
>rest the whole game)
>Longbow of Diana + 500 normal arrows (Never used one yet, 150 or so
>are from crossbow bolts dipped in a potion of polymorph)

If you haven't used the arrows at all, do I assume correctly your
skill hasn't been pushed up yet? If so, these aren't probably your
best bet.

>50 normal daggers (already enchanted to +4 and rustproofed)

These are great to have with any weapon. Chances are you can't quiver
all 50 at once, but it's nice to have extras. Charge 'em up to +6 or
+7 and quiver as many as you can stand to carry.

>Frostbrand (my best bet as a main weapon, but freezes useful healing
>potions)
>Grayswandir (stole it from a shop, stupid thing blasts me when I wield
>it)

Grayswandir rocks, but you can't get any skill in it. If you got
Werebane as a sacrifice, you can at least advance to Basic. Once
Grayswandir is nicely enchanted, it's a serious death-dealer (just
like Frost Brand, but with no potion dangers).

>Werebane (silver damage, obviously)
>Stormbringer (Got this only 2nd sacrafice, using it so far)

Stormy's not bad, but it can take a while against high-level monsters.
I personally would go with either FB or Grayswandir as main weapon
with a bunch of daggers in the quiver. Fire daggers for ranged damage
and hit 'em with the big guns as they close.

